    LLM: "For Beginners:\n1. Learn valid meld types (sequences and groups)\n2. Look for opportunities to add to existing melds\n3. Save jokers for difficult combinations\n4. Don't draw 3 cards unless you have no melding option\n\n1. Plan rearrangements before drawing\n2. Track which cards have been played\n3. Use jokers to release other jokers for reuse\n4. Time your knock carefully - check opponent likely scores\n\n1. Complex multi-step rearrangements to play multiple cards\n2. Block opponents by creating melds they cannot extend\n3. Calculate probabilities of drawing needed cards\n4. Endgame optimization for minimizing penalties",
